#! clause: E5.4
#! mode: run
#! requires: read_line
#! expect-out: hi
#! input: read_line -> "hi"
# The parity control for `reentry-001` (D-M7-1): the SAME shape — a consumer invoking a block whose
# body suspends — but the consumer is written in DOODLE. Doodle owns the loop, so the block's
# `read_line()` suspends the ordinary way and the host resolves it; no fault. This is the normative
# idiom for suspension inside iteration (E§5.4): expose the capability, let Doodle drive.
to consume(x, do body)
  body(x)
end
consume(1) do (n)
  print(read_line())
end
